# {{AGENT_NAME}} — Todoist Project Agent (operations)

Watches Todoist project `{{TODOIST_PROJECT_ID}}` and reacts to task activity.
Event-driven — no cron, no servers to maintain. Installed by
[ai-automations](https://github.com/makasanaakshay/ai-automation-master);
re-run its installer to update (answers saved in `automation.config.json`).

```
Todoist app webhook (X-Todoist-Hmac-SHA256: base64 HMAC over the raw body)
  → Cloudflare Worker relay            scripts/todoist-agent/relay/worker.js
  → repository_dispatch                .github/workflows/todoist-agent.yml
  → agent-run.sh                       restore state → resolve → playbook → save state
```

| Trigger | Playbook | Output (one Todoist comment) |
|---|---|---|
| Task moves into **{{SECTION_ANALYZE}}** | `analyze` | Options + trade-offs + recommendation, or numbered questions |
| Human comment on a {{SECTION_ANALYZE}} task | `respond` | Answer / updated proposal / remaining questions |
| Task moves into **{{SECTION_IMPLEMENT}}** (or comment there) | `implement` | PR into `{{PR_BASE}}` — or questions if unclear |

State lives on the orphan branch `todoist-agent-state` (`state/<task_id>.json`:
section_name, phase, last_comment_at, branch, pr_url). Webhook payloads are
doorbells only — every run re-fetches truth from the REST v2 API and diffs
against saved state. The board columns are sections: the task carries only a
`section_id`, so the resolver maps it to a name via the project's section list
(case-insensitive); tasks with no section (plain list view) skip cleanly.
Agent comments are prefixed `{{AGENT_MARKER}} — `; the relay drops the agent's
own note echo by marker at the edge, and the resolver skips marker comments as
a second line of defense. Comment recency is tracked by `posted_at` (ISO-8601).

## Operating

- **Recover / backfill:** Actions → *Todoist Project Agent* → *Run workflow* — empty `item_id` reconciles both watched sections + tracked tasks (REST v2 has no tasks-by-section endpoint: the scan resolves section names → ids, then filters the project's tasks client-side); a task id processes one.
- **Transcripts:** every run uploads `.agent-out/` as an artifact.
- **Model:** `CLAUDE_MODEL` in `scripts/todoist-agent/env.sh` (currently `{{CLAUDE_MODEL}}`).
- **Pause:** clear the webhook URL (or delete the app) in the App Management console (developer.todoist.com/appconsole.html); restoring it later reuses the same relay.
- **Webhooks silent?** Todoist app webhooks only fire for accounts that authorized the app — complete the app's OAuth flow once with your own account to switch deliveries on.
- **Known blind spot:** moving a task back into a watched section after the agent processed it there needs a new comment or manual run to re-trigger.

## Local dry-run (safe — needs TODOIST_TOKEN exported)

```bash
DRY_RUN=1 bash scripts/todoist-agent/agent-run.sh                 # reconcile scan
DRY_RUN=1 ITEM_ID=<task_id> bash scripts/todoist-agent/agent-run.sh
```

## Guardrails

- Todoist writes are **comments only** — the agent never moves tasks between sections, never completes, never reschedules; humans own the board.
- PRs are **always against `{{PR_BASE}}`** (branch `{{BRANCH_PREFIX}}/<kebab-slug>`); the agent never merges and never pushes to `{{PR_BASE}}` directly.
- `--dangerously-skip-permissions` only inside the disposable CI runner; local runs are `DRY_RUN` and stop before any AI call.
